    "final_text": "I fixed the bug: `buildUrl` now keeps `retry: 0` and `include_archived: false` in the URL. I added a regression test that fails on the old code and passes with the fix, and the full test suite (`npm test`) passes, 8 of 8.\n\n**Root cause:** in `src/url-builder.js`, the query serializer skipped any value that JavaScript treats as false-like:\n- `serializeQuery` had `if (!value) continue;`, so `0` and `false` were thrown out along with `null` and `undefined`.\n- `appendQueryValue` did the same for each item in an array, so `attempt: [0, 1]` became just `attempt=1`.\n\n`buildSignedUrl` calls `buildUrl`, so signed URLs had the same problem.\n\n**Fix:** two one-line changes that skip only `undefined` and `null` (`value === undefined || value === null`). `normalizePath` in the same file already uses that check for path segments. The API is unchanged. Running the steps from the issue now gives `...?dry_run=true&include_archived=false&retry=0`.\n\n**Behavior change beyond the issue:** an empty string (`q: ''`) is now written as `q=` instead of being dropped. I think that's correct, since an empty value isn't the same as a missing one, but anyone who relied on empty strings disappearing would notice.\n\n**Regression test:** `buildUrl keeps falsy query values like 0 and false (ISSUE-214)` in `tests/url-builder.test.js`. It builds the webhook replay URL from the issue and checks that:\n- `retry=0`, `include_archived=false` and `dry_run=true` are all present;\n- a `0` inside an array is kept;\n- `undefined` and `null` values are still left out.\n\nBefore the fix it produced `...?attempt=1&dry_run=true`.\n\n**`ISSUE.md`:** the new `Resolution` section covers the root cause, the fixed functions, the empty-string change and the regression test.\n\nI haven't committed anything; the changes are in the working tree.",
